  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nOur area will remain under the strong high pressure system \nbuilding off of the Four Corners region through the extended\nperiod. Monsoonal moisture influx will mainly stay south and \neast of our area, leading to hot, dry, and breezy conditions \nthroughout the long-term period. Temperatures will generally \nstay near normal Tuesday through Wednesday. By the end of the \nweek , the Four Corners high will begin to shift west and \namplify over the Great Basin, allowing for a warming trend to 5 \ndegrees above normal come Thursday and Friday. Saturday may see \na dry cold frontal passage that could return temperatures to \nnear normal.",
